  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of sustainability has evolved significantly over the past few decades. Initially, it was seen as a niche concern, primarily associated with environmental issues such as pollution and deforestation. However, in recent years, there has been a growing recognition that sustainability encompasses not only environmental considerations but also social and economic aspects.\n\nIn fact, many experts now argue that sustainable development is essential for the long-term survival of our planet. They point out that the world's resources are finite, and if we continue to consume them at the current rate, we will eventually run out. Moreover, the consequences of climate change, such as rising sea levels and extreme weather events, pose a significant threat to global stability.\n\nDespite these challenges, there is growing momentum towards sustainable development. Governments, businesses, and individuals are increasingly recognizing the need for more environmentally friendly practices. For instance, many companies are now adopting renewable energy sources, reducing waste, and promoting eco-friendly products.\n\nHowever, critics argue that the focus on sustainability has led to a 'greenwashing' phenomenon, where companies exaggerate their environmental credentials to improve their public image. This can be misleading and even damaging, as it may distract from genuine efforts towards sustainability.\n\nIn conclusion, while there are challenges ahead, the shift towards sustainable development is undoubtedly underway. It requires a collective effort from governments, businesses, and individuals to prioritize long-term thinking over short-term gains.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The concept of sustainability has been around for centuries.\", \"Sustainability encompasses environmental, social, and economic aspects.\", \"The world's resources are finite and will eventually run out.\", \"Greenwashing is a major obstacle to sustainable development.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Sustainability encompasses environmental, social, and economic aspects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the passage, what is one of the consequences of climate change?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Rising sea levels\", \"Extreme weather events\", \"Polar ice caps melting\", \"All of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Extreme weather events\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'greenwashing' refer to in the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The practice of using renewable energy sources.\", \"Companies exaggerating their environmental credentials for public image improvement.\", \"Eco-friendly products becoming more widely available.\", \"Governments prioritizing long-term thinking over short-term gains.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Companies exaggerating their environmental credentials for public image improvement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"The passage suggests that sustainable development requires a collective effort from which groups?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Governments and businesses only\", \"Individuals, governments, and businesses\", \"Environmental organizations and scientists only\", \"Companies adopting renewable energy sources\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Individuals, governments, and businesses\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards sustainable development is best described as?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Cautious and pessimistic\", \"Optimistic but critical\", \"Neutral and informative\", \"Ambitious and idealistic\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Optimistic but critical\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
